{"The group/members.hbs template iterates {{#each m in members}}, but the route sets the Group object as the controller model and calls model.findMembers() without awaiting it, so on first render members is undefined and the member list renders empty": 0.817439615726471, "Admin group member pagination can compute an extra page and advance offset to user_count, causing the UI to navigate to a page that returns zero members when user_count is an exact multiple of limit or after a removal reduces total while keeping offset at the old boundary": 0.622365415096283, "The test for 'cannot remove members from automatic groups' uses xhr :put, :remove_member but the route is defined as delete 'members' => 'groups#remove_member', so the test exercises the wrong action and does not validate the intended behavior": 0.9295674562454224, "In remove_member, group.users.delete(user_id) passes a raw integer to delete on a has_many :through association, but Rails' CollectionProxy#delete expects ActiveRecord objects, causing member removal to silently fail or raise an error": 0.798678994178772}